\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>One night, Chanta woke from disturbing, fitful dreams and blinked at what appeared to be a continuation of the same nightmare. An old man with a long grey beard and crazed hair, dressed in full leathers, stood at the foot of his bed. Chanta ignored the apparition until it spoke:\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Don\'92t despair, young Tony.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Life\'92s taxed,\'94 Chanta mumbled into his pillow, \'93then you lose the only ray of sunshine that\'92s ever blessed your Cloudborne head.\'94 His eyelids felt like the Layer squatting on them.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Chantara!\'94 the apparition wheezed, louder than a whisper. \'93Get your tax together. We\'92re depending on you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta blinked and reassessed the ghost. \'93Hang on, I know you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The ghost stepped from the shadows and handed Chanta a business card.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I can\'92t read this in the dark,\'94 Chanta complained. The lamp on the bedside table went unnoticed\'97he wasn\'92t used to having one that worked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Allow me to introduce myself. I\'92m Solon Athena, Prophecy Facilitator of Seven Sages Corp. 
\f2\i Don\'92t call us\'97heroes are called.
\f1\i0 \'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Good. I didn\'92t call you. So tax off.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Young Tony, I know things seem dark now.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Don\'92t you turn a light on. I sleep buff, you know.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Apologies. I didn\'92t know that.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Some prophecy fac-silly-tater.\'94 Chanta rolled on his side, snuggled into a second pillow.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You are fundamental to the fruition of the prophecy. You will become a great influencer.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta yawned. \'93Great influencer, great teacher, great sandwich-maker\'85 I\'92m none of those things. I\'92m a fraud, and when the Elvi figure it out, they\'92ll throw me out on the street. None of it matters anyway, not without Sarah.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93But Tony, Sarah has her own role to play. You will be reconciled, in time, I promise you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta\'92s eyes opened. He turned the possibility over in his mind.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I will see Sarah again?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Indubitably.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta sat up, alert. \'93In Dubai, what? Sarah\'92s in Dubai? Has she been kidnapped again?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No, no\'97I only mean\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93How do you know I\'92ll see her again? Is it in the prophecy?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Indubi\'97most certainly.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Then you want to make it happen\'85\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Solo wavered. \'93Not exactly, but it is my duty to do everything in my power to bring it about.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Like you had a hand in getting her pregnant.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Solo looked at the floor. \'93Not one of our finest moments. Chilo is\'85\'94 he searched for the words. \'93Spartan. Militaristic.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93But 
\f2\i you\'92re
\f1\i0  working to bring us back together.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is part of the meaning and purpose of my whole life.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Good. Now tax off and let me sleep.\'94
